1
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:05,760
You're roommates, so I don't mind.

2
00:00:05,840 --> 00:00:07,600
But you're not dating, right?

3
00:00:07,680 --> 00:00:09,720
This week's club mission is to help him.

4
00:00:09,800 --> 00:00:10,960
You need something new.

5
00:00:11,040 --> 00:00:12,160
Once you try something new,

6
00:00:12,240 --> 00:00:13,480
it'll be easier to forget the past.

7
00:00:13,560 --> 00:00:14,560
Don't lose to the voice in your head.

8
00:00:14,640 --> 00:00:15,720
I made that rule myself.

9
00:00:15,800 --> 00:00:17,680
And he already likes someone.

10
00:00:17,760 --> 00:00:18,800
Don't you feel anything at all?

11
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:24,160
What inspired you to confess to Summer?

12
00:00:24,240 --> 00:00:27,200
<i>It may sound cliché,</i>
<i>but I'd regret it if I never told her.</i>

13
00:00:27,280 --> 00:00:30,680
<i>I like you.</i>
<i>Break the rule and be my boyfriend.</i>

14
00:00:30,760 --> 00:00:32,040
<i>Will you open your heart to me?</i>

15
00:00:33,360 --> 00:00:34,280
As my boyfriend.

16
00:00:38,760 --> 00:00:40,680
<i>Go for it. Charge in!</i>

17
00:00:40,760 --> 00:00:43,240
- <i>Go!</i>
- <i>Hey! Down there!</i>

18
00:00:43,320 --> 00:00:44,720
<i>Hey! Ter! Ter!</i>

19
00:00:44,800 --> 00:00:45,720
<i>He's going down!</i>

20
00:00:45,800 --> 00:00:46,720
Yeah, that's it! Nice!

21
00:00:46,800 --> 00:00:48,320
Nice! We've got the advantage!

22
00:00:48,400 --> 00:00:50,600
- Hit him! Hit him!
- Ter! Down there!

23
00:00:50,680 --> 00:00:53,600
- <i>He's in! He's in!</i>
- He's going for the kill!

24
00:00:53,680 --> 00:00:55,680
<i>That's it! That's it!</i>

25
00:00:55,760 --> 00:00:57,920
Ter is on fire.

26
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:00,320
I totally ship them. They're even
using the same Discord account.

27
00:01:00,400 --> 00:01:02,040
Even Leo and Neo use separate accounts.

28
00:01:02,120 --> 00:01:04,120
Come on, damn it. Let us have some space.

29
00:01:04,200 --> 00:01:05,560
We're practically glued together 24/7.

30
00:01:07,960 --> 00:01:09,240
Yeah,

31
00:01:09,320 --> 00:01:11,320
- this is my last game.
- Mine too.

32
00:01:11,960 --> 00:01:13,040
This is my last match too.

33
00:01:16,600 --> 00:01:17,440
What's with you?

34
00:01:18,040 --> 00:01:19,320
If you're sleepy, just sleep here.

35
00:01:20,040 --> 00:01:21,440
We've been dating for less than a month,

36
00:01:21,520 --> 00:01:22,440
and you're already asking me
to sleep with you.

37
00:01:23,040 --> 00:01:24,160
You idiot.

38
00:01:24,240 --> 00:01:26,520
What are you thinking?
I just meant sleeping.

39
00:01:27,480 --> 00:01:29,680
Wait until we've been together for a year,
then I'll sleep with you.

40
00:01:30,600 --> 00:01:32,120
You're so damn adorable.

41
00:01:33,280 --> 00:01:34,480
LeeIth, that's enough.

42
00:01:37,120 --> 00:01:38,120
Where are you going?

43
00:01:39,480 --> 00:01:41,520
Just act natural
when we go to school tomorrow.

44
00:01:42,120 --> 00:01:43,720
Then let me get my fill of you first.

45
00:01:44,440 --> 00:01:45,280
Get your fill of what?

46
00:01:48,480 --> 00:01:49,560
That's enough.

47
00:01:50,480 --> 00:01:51,680
Hey, that's enough.

48
00:01:51,760 --> 00:01:52,880
You're acting like a dog.

49
00:01:52,960 --> 00:01:54,520
Stop. You're acting like a dog.

50
00:01:54,600 --> 00:01:56,360
- That's enough.
- That's because I'm your puppy.

51
00:01:56,440 --> 00:01:58,640
LeeIth! Ter! Hello? Are you guys there?

52
00:01:59,320 --> 00:02:00,480
<i>Come on, put in some effort.</i>

53
00:02:00,560 --> 00:02:01,520
<i>Hello?</i>

54
00:02:01,600 --> 00:02:03,120
<i>Hey, don't go quiet, asshole.</i>

55
00:02:03,200 --> 00:02:05,040
<i>You two aren't doing something, are you?</i>

56
00:02:05,920 --> 00:02:07,400
I just went to take a leak, and…

57
00:02:07,480 --> 00:02:08,680
Ter's going to bed.

58
00:02:08,759 --> 00:02:10,639
Nothing's going on. Nothing…

59
00:02:12,320 --> 00:02:13,320
I'm off to bed, guys.

60
00:02:13,400 --> 00:02:14,480
- Okay, bye.
- Okay.

61
00:02:14,560 --> 00:02:15,760
- See you.
- Okay.

62
00:02:17,160 --> 00:02:18,240
I'm going to bed.

63
00:02:19,800 --> 00:02:20,960
Sweet dreams.

64
00:02:22,920 --> 00:02:24,320
Remember to act natural tomorrow.

65
00:02:24,400 --> 00:02:27,160
- Got it?
- Okay, you should go now.

66
00:02:27,240 --> 00:02:28,520
- Bye.
- Sweet dreams.

67
00:02:28,600 --> 00:02:29,600
Sweet dreams.

68
00:02:32,600 --> 00:02:34,240
That hit way too hard.

69
00:02:34,320 --> 00:02:35,960
How am I supposed to survive this?

70
00:02:40,760 --> 00:02:43,320
You're taking the fitness test.
Stay focused.

71
00:02:43,400 --> 00:02:44,400
Yes, Sir.

72
00:02:50,840 --> 00:02:52,120
Okay.

73
00:03:04,160 --> 00:03:06,280
Stop. Someone will see us.

74
00:03:07,040 --> 00:03:08,280
Putter.

75
00:03:09,440 --> 00:03:11,440
Where are you rushing off to?

76
00:03:13,480 --> 00:03:14,480
Huh?

77
00:03:15,680 --> 00:03:17,200
You're acting weird.

78
00:03:17,280 --> 00:03:19,320
Did something happen during the break?

79
00:03:19,400 --> 00:03:21,160
Why do you look so cheerful?

80
00:03:21,240 --> 00:03:23,560
Yeah. Are you in love or something?

81
00:03:25,240 --> 00:03:28,120
What? I just saw something funny.

82
00:03:29,600 --> 00:03:31,480
- What was so funny?
- Yeah, what was so funny?

83
00:03:43,840 --> 00:03:45,200
Hey, I need to pee.

84
00:03:46,080 --> 00:03:47,440
Then pee.

85
00:03:47,520 --> 00:03:48,760
I've already seen it all.

86
00:03:53,640 --> 00:03:54,800
What the hell are you doing?

87
00:03:54,880 --> 00:03:56,640
I'm here to take a shower.

88
00:03:57,240 --> 00:03:58,880
What are you embarrassed about?
I've got one too.

89
00:03:58,960 --> 00:04:00,520
Hey, idiot! Get out!

90
00:04:08,280 --> 00:04:10,040
Don't forget to fix the door lock.

91
00:04:14,480 --> 00:04:15,480
It doesn't need fixing.

92
00:04:16,720 --> 00:04:19,079
No need to lock it. We're dating now.

93
00:04:20,560 --> 00:04:23,280
Even if we're dating,
shouldn't we still have some boundaries?

94
00:04:24,160 --> 00:04:26,160
Okay, my boyfriend.

95
00:04:26,840 --> 00:04:29,080
Move aside. I need to dry my hands.

96
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:55,800
Go pee too, LeeIth.

97
00:04:55,880 --> 00:04:56,880
Yeah, coming.

98
00:05:18,120 --> 00:05:19,080
Move.

99
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:23,120
- Move over.
- Yeah, scoot over.

100
00:05:23,200 --> 00:05:25,600
Damn, you two took forever in there.

101
00:05:25,680 --> 00:05:27,320
What the hell were you guys doing?

102
00:05:36,560 --> 00:05:38,080
What?

103
00:05:38,160 --> 00:05:39,480
Is spending a long time
in the bathroom a crime?

104
00:05:45,520 --> 00:05:47,360
- What the hell are you looking at?
- You wanna go?

105
00:05:47,440 --> 00:05:48,960
- Asshole.
- You looking for a fight?

106
00:05:49,040 --> 00:05:51,480
- You wanna fight?
- You wanna go?

107
00:05:54,920 --> 00:05:56,240
Get him!

108
00:07:26,600 --> 00:07:27,600
I'm starving.

109
00:07:27,680 --> 00:07:28,720
Where's your twin?

110
00:07:28,800 --> 00:07:29,880
Where'd the other one go?

111
00:07:30,640 --> 00:07:31,680
He's shy around girls.

112
00:07:31,760 --> 00:07:34,960
He's over there eating by himself.

113
00:07:38,520 --> 00:07:40,000
I have a plan.

114
00:07:40,080 --> 00:07:42,280
- Huh? What?
- I know what to do.

115
00:07:42,360 --> 00:07:45,000
Hey, Leo. My friends have forgiven you.

116
00:07:45,080 --> 00:07:46,360
You're welcome to join us at our table.

117
00:07:46,440 --> 00:07:48,440
Or should we come eat with you?

118
00:07:48,520 --> 00:07:50,480
How about it? Go on, go.

119
00:07:50,560 --> 00:07:51,960
Go on. Go.

120
00:07:52,040 --> 00:07:54,680
I'll go myself. Hang on.

121
00:07:54,760 --> 00:07:56,760
- He's coming.
- It actually worked.

122
00:07:58,480 --> 00:07:59,840
- Hey.
- Sit here, dumbass.

123
00:07:59,920 --> 00:08:01,240
- We're all friends.
- Have a seat.

124
00:08:01,320 --> 00:08:02,920
Hi.

125
00:08:03,720 --> 00:08:05,640
I'll sit somewhere else.

126
00:08:07,120 --> 00:08:08,600
- He's really shy.
- Told you.

127
00:08:08,680 --> 00:08:12,320
- He's ridiculously shy.
- Your delivery is here.

128
00:08:12,400 --> 00:08:14,400
You're so sweet. Thank you.

129
00:08:16,200 --> 00:08:17,640
Guys, come here.

130
00:08:18,840 --> 00:08:21,240
When did those two make up?

131
00:08:22,200 --> 00:08:23,600
After the concert at Siam,

132
00:08:23,680 --> 00:08:25,840
they made a huge public apology
to each other online.

133
00:08:26,960 --> 00:08:28,760
Classic.

134
00:08:28,840 --> 00:08:30,040
Same old ending.

135
00:08:30,880 --> 00:08:32,400
Hey,

136
00:08:32,480 --> 00:08:34,440
you're gossiping right in front of us.

137
00:08:34,520 --> 00:08:36,559
We weren't gossiping, were we?

138
00:08:36,640 --> 00:08:39,440
Nobody was gossiping.
We were just keeping everyone informed.

139
00:08:39,520 --> 00:08:41,400
Just making sure everyone knows.

140
00:08:43,559 --> 00:08:44,760
Oh, right, Proud.

141
00:08:44,840 --> 00:08:45,840
I never got to tell you.

142
00:08:45,920 --> 00:08:46,920
You were so cool that day.

143
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:48,160
Thanks, Indy.

144
00:08:48,240 --> 00:08:50,040
- Let's hang out together sometime.
- Sure.

145
00:08:51,040 --> 00:08:52,040
What? You want to steal her from me?

146
00:08:52,720 --> 00:08:53,760
Hey, hey!

147
00:08:53,840 --> 00:08:55,800
BeReal, everyone! BeReal!

148
00:08:57,040 --> 00:08:59,240
- Here we go.
- Okay, one, two, three.

149
00:09:00,960 --> 00:09:01,960
Okay.

150
00:09:02,800 --> 00:09:04,680
- What is that?
- So cute.

151
00:09:06,080 --> 00:09:07,120
What is it?

152
00:09:08,280 --> 00:09:11,280
It's kind of like Instagram.
You explain it.

153
00:09:11,360 --> 00:09:13,240
It randomly gives you a two-minute timer

154
00:09:13,320 --> 00:09:15,160
to take a real, unfiltered photo.

155
00:09:15,240 --> 00:09:17,040
It uses both the front
and rear cameras at the same time

156
00:09:17,120 --> 00:09:18,320
to capture the moment as a memory.

157
00:09:19,200 --> 00:09:20,920
You're so smart, babe.

158
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:22,080
Do guys use it too?

159
00:09:22,160 --> 00:09:24,040
It was huge for a while.

160
00:09:24,120 --> 00:09:26,400
It's not as popular now,

161
00:09:26,480 --> 00:09:28,160
but it's still pretty good.

162
00:09:28,240 --> 00:09:30,080
- Bring your food over here.
- It captures little moments.

163
00:09:30,160 --> 00:09:31,640
You don't have to order
the same thing as me next time.

164
00:09:31,720 --> 00:09:33,160
I didn't copy you. I always order this.

165
00:09:33,240 --> 00:09:35,000
Then why'd you bring
your food over if you didn't?

166
00:09:36,320 --> 00:09:37,600
Are you seriously just eating rice?

167
00:09:37,680 --> 00:09:39,760
- Yeah, this is enough for me.
- Come on, don't argue.

168
00:09:41,120 --> 00:09:42,320
What did you bring?

169
00:09:47,760 --> 00:09:49,720
- What's that?
- Looks delicious.

170
00:09:49,800 --> 00:09:50,960
Is that healthy food?

171
00:09:51,040 --> 00:09:52,120
- Did you make it yourself?
- It looks so good.

172
00:09:54,680 --> 00:09:56,800
- You're amazing.
- That's good.

173
00:09:56,880 --> 00:09:59,080
This is way better
than your blended chicken breast.

174
00:09:59,160 --> 00:10:00,800
It makes me want to throw up
every time I see it.

175
00:10:00,880 --> 00:10:02,000
Why would you say that?

176
00:10:02,080 --> 00:10:04,080
Seriously, it's really good.

177
00:10:04,160 --> 00:10:06,320
Go ahead. Here's the chicken breast dish.

178
00:10:07,360 --> 00:10:09,160
What do you think, Chef? Give it a try.

179
00:10:12,920 --> 00:10:14,120
How is it?

180
00:10:15,600 --> 00:10:16,440
Nine out of ten.

181
00:10:16,520 --> 00:10:17,880
Hey, what about the last point?

182
00:10:17,960 --> 00:10:19,760
If I give you a perfect score,
you'll get cocky.

183
00:10:20,800 --> 00:10:22,000
Okay, fair enough.

184
00:10:23,640 --> 00:10:25,200
Isn't it a bit bland?

185
00:10:26,640 --> 00:10:29,440
Come on, hurry up. Eat it.

186
00:10:29,520 --> 00:10:30,600
Let me have some too.

187
00:10:31,760 --> 00:10:32,880
- I'll take this piece.
- Can you make this for me sometime?

188
00:10:32,960 --> 00:10:35,440
Are the vegetables cooked?
LeeIth, give them a try.

189
00:10:35,520 --> 00:10:36,720
I'm good.

190
00:10:36,800 --> 00:10:38,240
I don't want to steal Ter's food.

191
00:10:38,800 --> 00:10:40,080
You can tell it's good
just by looking at it.

192
00:10:41,880 --> 00:10:43,080
Then I'll eat it myself.

193
00:10:43,160 --> 00:10:44,080
Yeah, me too.

194
00:10:45,880 --> 00:10:48,280
Actually, it's still a little undercooked.

195
00:10:48,840 --> 00:10:50,200
True.

196
00:10:50,280 --> 00:10:52,600
- You're right.
- The vegetables are really bland.

197
00:10:52,680 --> 00:10:54,480
Hey, don't be discouraged.

198
00:10:54,560 --> 00:10:56,000
I actually like it this way.

199
00:11:06,120 --> 00:11:08,160
Alright. Werewolves, open your eyes.

200
00:11:12,760 --> 00:11:14,920
I can tell.
Indy definitely opened his eyes.

201
00:11:16,560 --> 00:11:17,680
Then prove it.

202
00:11:19,440 --> 00:11:21,360
I don't believe you. Just wait and see.

203
00:11:21,440 --> 00:11:22,520
That's enough, you guys.

204
00:11:23,240 --> 00:11:24,680
Werewolves, close your eyes.

205
00:11:26,240 --> 00:11:29,240
Seer, open your eyes.

206
00:11:30,640 --> 00:11:32,160
Who would you like to check
on the first night?

207
00:11:39,280 --> 00:11:40,360
But…

208
00:11:46,800 --> 00:11:49,360
Seer, stop taking so long. Hurry up.

209
00:11:49,440 --> 00:11:50,400
I'm about to fall asleep, damn it.

210
00:11:52,160 --> 00:11:53,480
Seer, close your eyes.

211
00:11:53,560 --> 00:11:54,840
Done, done, done.

212
00:11:54,920 --> 00:11:56,560
Alright, everyone, open your eyes.

213
00:11:59,320 --> 00:12:01,000
The werewolves win.

214
00:12:05,160 --> 00:12:06,880
Damn, I can't trust anyone.

215
00:12:06,960 --> 00:12:08,840
- You're so sneaky.
- I lost all eight rounds.

216
00:12:10,520 --> 00:12:12,400
How am I supposed
to trust you guys after this?

217
00:12:12,480 --> 00:12:15,040
You guys are so good at lying.
I don't want to play anymore.

218
00:12:15,120 --> 00:12:16,680
- Me neither.
- I'm innocent.

219
00:12:16,760 --> 00:12:18,200
I was the moderator.

220
00:12:19,320 --> 00:12:21,080
You sneaky little bastard.

221
00:12:21,160 --> 00:12:23,000
- Never saw that coming.
- Time's up, isn't it?

222
00:12:24,440 --> 00:12:26,480
School's giving us tomorrow off
for exam prep.

223
00:12:26,560 --> 00:12:28,240
Where are you guys studying?

224
00:12:28,320 --> 00:12:29,560
Should we study together?

225
00:12:29,640 --> 00:12:31,320
LeeIth and I always form a study group.

226
00:12:31,400 --> 00:12:34,120
Damn, every time I come here,

227
00:12:34,200 --> 00:12:36,200
we never actually study.
We just mess around.

228
00:12:36,280 --> 00:12:38,600
It's called study-life balance.

229
00:12:40,200 --> 00:12:42,240
Hey, this time I want to study at home.

230
00:12:42,320 --> 00:12:45,040
My mom will kill me otherwise.
You're such a wimp.

231
00:12:45,120 --> 00:12:47,400
Let's wait and study together
for finals instead.

232
00:12:48,920 --> 00:12:51,160
- No, no, no.
- Calm down.

233
00:12:51,240 --> 00:12:53,000
We're outside. Take it easy.

234
00:12:53,080 --> 00:12:54,360
What about you, Ter?

235
00:12:59,320 --> 00:13:00,520
I'll just study at home.

236
00:13:01,600 --> 00:13:02,600
I get distracted easily.

237
00:13:04,200 --> 00:13:05,200
That's depressing.

238
00:13:06,600 --> 00:13:08,200
Come on, one more round.

239
00:13:08,280 --> 00:13:10,440
Now that you're over your heartbreak,
you're all fired up.

240
00:13:10,520 --> 00:13:12,000
Are you making fun of me?

241
00:13:12,080 --> 00:13:13,160
Easy, easy.

242
00:13:13,240 --> 00:13:14,680
- Calm down, Bro.
- Easy, easy.

243
00:13:15,720 --> 00:13:17,400
Hey, hey. I'm sorry.

244
00:13:17,480 --> 00:13:19,720
- I'm sorry.
- Don't fight.

245
00:13:19,800 --> 00:13:21,560
Come on!

246
00:13:25,560 --> 00:13:26,960
I'm bored.

247
00:13:41,800 --> 00:13:42,800
That's BeReal.

248
00:13:44,480 --> 00:13:46,240
Why didn't you tell everyone you use it?

249
00:13:46,880 --> 00:13:48,160
Because I wanted to keep it to myself.

250
00:13:50,560 --> 00:13:51,840
Hey.

251
00:13:51,920 --> 00:13:53,160
Take a picture of me.

252
00:13:53,240 --> 00:13:56,720
- Come on, take one of me. Hurry.
- Yeah, sure.

253
00:14:05,720 --> 00:14:07,640
Damn. Too real.

254
00:14:08,440 --> 00:14:09,440
Let me see.

255
00:14:13,800 --> 00:14:15,960
Yep, that's totally me.

256
00:14:21,960 --> 00:14:23,320
You've been using it for a long time.

257
00:14:24,920 --> 00:14:26,840
Yeah. Since before
I transferred to this school.

258
00:14:27,920 --> 00:14:28,960
Huh?

259
00:14:29,040 --> 00:14:30,400
Was this from the first day of school?

260
00:14:30,480 --> 00:14:31,680
This one.

261
00:14:32,280 --> 00:14:33,920
- Look, look.
- You remember?

262
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:39,600
Well, meeting someone like you…

263
00:14:40,480 --> 00:14:41,680
isn't something I'd forget.

264
00:14:42,960 --> 00:14:45,200
- Was I cute?
- Yeah.

265
00:14:46,480 --> 00:14:48,760
You're not even going to play along?

266
00:14:50,680 --> 00:14:51,680
Then set it up again.

267
00:14:53,120 --> 00:14:55,280
So… Was I cute?

268
00:14:56,440 --> 00:14:57,400
Yeah.

269
00:15:00,440 --> 00:15:02,080
What's with you?

270
00:15:02,160 --> 00:15:03,360
You're so whipped.

271
00:15:03,440 --> 00:15:06,360
So, when are you actually going to study?

272
00:15:10,920 --> 00:15:11,760
That hurt.

273
00:15:12,320 --> 00:15:13,160
What was that for?

274
00:15:13,240 --> 00:15:14,720
When, then?

275
00:15:14,800 --> 00:15:16,440
How's anything going to stick
if you don't study?

276
00:15:16,520 --> 00:15:19,240
You ditched your friends,
and you're still not studying.

277
00:15:19,320 --> 00:15:21,320
Go check the CCTV footage.

278
00:15:21,400 --> 00:15:23,920
I said I'd study at home,

279
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:25,720
but I never said I'd study seriously.

280
00:15:33,160 --> 00:15:34,840
Studying at home…

281
00:15:35,880 --> 00:15:37,760
really is more comfortable
than studying outside.

282
00:15:48,120 --> 00:15:49,560
What's with you?

283
00:15:51,920 --> 00:15:53,240
Is that a new perfume?

284
00:15:54,600 --> 00:15:56,160
Yeah. What do you think?

285
00:15:59,160 --> 00:16:00,440
Well, it's new.

286
00:16:00,520 --> 00:16:02,560
But your old one was more popular.

287
00:16:03,080 --> 00:16:04,520
Indy uses this one too.

288
00:16:08,040 --> 00:16:09,480
Can you even solve these problems?

289
00:16:10,360 --> 00:16:12,880
I have no idea. Can you teach me?

290
00:16:13,600 --> 00:16:16,160
- Yeah. Come down and I'll teach you.
- No.

291
00:16:18,640 --> 00:16:20,800
Come down here. Come on.

292
00:16:20,880 --> 00:16:22,760
Can you get down properly?

293
00:16:24,760 --> 00:16:26,000
Come on.

294
00:16:29,440 --> 00:16:30,360
Watch me.

295
00:16:30,440 --> 00:16:32,280
See this one? See this problem?

296
00:16:32,360 --> 00:16:34,320
You solve it the same way.

297
00:16:34,400 --> 00:16:35,360
You'll get this.

298
00:16:40,520 --> 00:16:44,080
I never thought
I'd end up living with a genius.

299
00:16:44,160 --> 00:16:46,760
At first, all you did was play games
and draw all day.

300
00:16:47,920 --> 00:16:49,680
I never thought you'd be this smart.

301
00:16:52,000 --> 00:16:54,200
You're so dramatic.

302
00:16:54,280 --> 00:16:55,960
Seriously, so dramatic.

303
00:16:56,040 --> 00:16:57,840
- So dramatic.
- Yeah.

304
00:16:58,640 --> 00:17:00,160
I am dramatic.

305
00:17:10,200 --> 00:17:11,839
These days,

306
00:17:12,440 --> 00:17:13,960
you've got quite a sweet tooth.

307
00:17:14,040 --> 00:17:15,720
Keep it up, and they'll have to
amputate your leg.

308
00:17:16,960 --> 00:17:19,160
Whenever I say something, I mean it.

309
00:17:19,240 --> 00:17:21,160
Someone like you

310
00:17:21,240 --> 00:17:22,560
could easily become a doctor.

311
00:17:22,640 --> 00:17:24,119
Whoa, a doctor?

312
00:17:24,680 --> 00:17:25,760
Damn.

313
00:17:26,480 --> 00:17:28,160
That never even crossed my mind.

314
00:17:30,120 --> 00:17:32,720
So, why did you choose architecture?

315
00:17:35,280 --> 00:17:37,840
Honestly,
I wanted to become an esports player.

316
00:17:38,520 --> 00:17:40,920
But my family is all about art,

317
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:42,360
so I had to study architecture.

318
00:17:43,480 --> 00:17:44,560
That makes sense.

319
00:17:45,240 --> 00:17:47,080
I have to study engineering
because of my dad too.

320
00:17:49,960 --> 00:17:52,000
That's why I wanted to study in Bangkok.

321
00:17:52,080 --> 00:17:53,760
I wanted to get away from them.

322
00:17:54,280 --> 00:17:56,000
When you're chasing your dream,

323
00:17:56,080 --> 00:17:57,960
having to hide it all the time…

324
00:17:58,040 --> 00:17:59,280
is suffocating.

325
00:18:00,640 --> 00:18:01,840
From now on,

326
00:18:02,360 --> 00:18:04,440
I'll be your number one supporter

327
00:18:04,520 --> 00:18:06,280
and your very first fan.

328
00:18:07,080 --> 00:18:09,200
I'll be cheering you on
at every match from the front row.

329
00:18:10,880 --> 00:18:12,720
You're so dramatic.

330
00:18:12,800 --> 00:18:14,880
Seriously, so dramatic.

331
00:18:14,960 --> 00:18:16,600
Now I'm getting you back.

332
00:18:19,280 --> 00:18:20,240
I mean every word.

333
00:18:20,320 --> 00:18:21,960
Jaguar FireStorm.

334
00:18:34,560 --> 00:18:35,560
Idiot.

335
00:18:56,320 --> 00:19:00,560
MIDTERM EXAM DAY

336
00:19:05,680 --> 00:19:06,640
So,

337
00:19:06,720 --> 00:19:09,400
- How did the exam go?
- I'm definitely getting an A.

338
00:19:10,000 --> 00:19:11,240
Because I had a great tutor.

339
00:19:11,320 --> 00:19:12,480
And he's cute too.

340
00:19:15,360 --> 00:19:16,920
Cut out the cheesy lines.

341
00:19:18,120 --> 00:19:20,960
I'm definitely getting a high score.
Oh, right.

342
00:19:21,040 --> 00:19:23,440
Don't forget the reward.
We promised we'd go on a trip.

343
00:19:24,920 --> 00:19:28,040
Exams are finally over! Time to celebrate!

344
00:19:28,120 --> 00:19:29,800
- Let's grab something to eat.
- What should we eat?

345
00:19:29,880 --> 00:19:31,720
- Let's go eat. I'm starving.
- Let's go.

346
00:19:31,800 --> 00:19:33,320
- Where should we go?
- I'm starving already. Huh?

347
00:19:33,400 --> 00:19:34,840
Anywhere's fine. Let's go.

348
00:19:36,400 --> 00:19:37,480
Hurry up.

349
00:19:37,560 --> 00:19:39,120
I'm starving. That exam was brutal.

350
00:19:39,200 --> 00:19:43,240
- Your salmon dish is ready.
- I ordered that.

351
00:19:43,320 --> 00:19:44,840
- I ordered one too.
- I'm having some too.

352
00:19:44,920 --> 00:19:46,960
- Dig in.
- Finish it all.

353
00:19:48,600 --> 00:19:49,840
- What?
- Top it up for me.

354
00:19:50,800 --> 00:19:52,280
Thanks.

355
00:19:52,360 --> 00:19:55,400
Don't let Min see you doing that,
or she'll totally ship you two.

356
00:19:55,480 --> 00:19:56,520
Who mentioned me?

357
00:19:56,600 --> 00:19:58,560
- Nothing.
- Nothing. Never mind.

358
00:19:58,640 --> 00:20:00,240
So cute.

359
00:20:00,320 --> 00:20:03,040
- Want another bite?
- I even told Goddess Lakshmi.

360
00:20:03,120 --> 00:20:04,000
About who?

361
00:20:04,080 --> 00:20:05,720
About you, of course.

362
00:20:05,800 --> 00:20:07,720
There's only one person.

363
00:20:08,680 --> 00:20:09,640
I'm going to the restroom.

364
00:20:09,720 --> 00:20:10,920
Go ahead.

365
00:20:15,160 --> 00:20:18,360
- Let me have some.
- Me too.

366
00:20:18,440 --> 00:20:20,080
Dear customers,

367
00:20:20,160 --> 00:20:22,200
today we have salmon on special.

368
00:20:22,280 --> 00:20:23,240
Raise your hand if you'd like one.

369
00:20:23,320 --> 00:20:26,560
- Me! Me!
- Me! Me!

370
00:20:26,640 --> 00:20:29,440
- Me first!
- Indy, don't you like sashimi?

371
00:20:30,600 --> 00:20:31,640
- I do.
- Then order it.

372
00:20:31,720 --> 00:20:33,080
But I don't eat salmon.

373
00:20:33,160 --> 00:20:34,920
Oh, right. I forgot.

374
00:20:36,480 --> 00:20:38,080
Should we order one for Ter?

375
00:20:38,160 --> 00:20:41,400
- In case he wants some.
- No, he doesn't eat salmon.

376
00:20:42,600 --> 00:20:43,560
Do you want one too?

377
00:20:43,640 --> 00:20:46,280
- No, I'm full.
- Okay.

378
00:20:48,480 --> 00:20:51,400
- You're pretty close to Ter, huh?
- Oh, my life.

379
00:20:51,480 --> 00:20:53,080
You even know what he likes.

380
00:20:53,160 --> 00:20:54,920
I just saw you guys arguing earlier.

381
00:20:55,000 --> 00:20:57,640
Well, we're roommates, aren't we?

382
00:20:57,720 --> 00:20:59,120
So I know him pretty well.

383
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:01,000
Really?

384
00:21:02,160 --> 00:21:03,160
Yeah.

385
00:21:10,080 --> 00:21:11,360
That's a lot. You eat so much.

386
00:21:12,400 --> 00:21:14,520
- Move over a bit.
- Come sit in here.

387
00:21:14,600 --> 00:21:15,720
Come sit here.

388
00:21:23,320 --> 00:21:24,320
Thanks.

389
00:21:53,200 --> 00:21:54,480
Hello.

390
00:21:56,640 --> 00:21:58,240
Um…

391
00:21:58,840 --> 00:21:59,920
Could you read my fortune?

392
00:22:02,280 --> 00:22:03,440
The shrine is closed today.

393
00:22:04,400 --> 00:22:06,480
I'll pay you. Double.

394
00:22:07,480 --> 00:22:08,840
Please.

395
00:22:13,240 --> 00:22:14,280
Come in.

396
00:22:29,080 --> 00:22:30,680
I can only read your fortune.

397
00:22:30,760 --> 00:22:33,120
I just want to know…

398
00:22:33,680 --> 00:22:35,400
who's going to confess to Ter…

399
00:22:36,000 --> 00:22:37,000
I can only read your fortune.

400
00:22:37,080 --> 00:22:39,160
…or who he has a crush on.

401
00:22:40,080 --> 00:22:41,400
I…

402
00:22:41,480 --> 00:22:43,720
can only read your fortune.

403
00:22:45,680 --> 00:22:46,960
What about Lee?

404
00:22:51,600 --> 00:22:52,800
If I say one more word,
I'll have to charge extra.

405
00:22:54,120 --> 00:22:55,880
I CAN ONLY READ YOUR FORTUNE.

406
00:23:02,920 --> 00:23:05,000
How about I read your overall
fortune instead?

407
00:23:22,440 --> 00:23:24,800
Lately, you've been lonely.
And feeling hurt.

408
00:23:24,880 --> 00:23:26,000
And paranoid.

409
00:23:26,680 --> 00:23:28,520
Damn, that's spot on.

410
00:23:28,600 --> 00:23:30,280
And The Moon card also says…

411
00:23:30,360 --> 00:23:32,920
you're overthinking,
so be careful with that.

412
00:23:41,960 --> 00:23:42,960
As for this one, I'd better not tell you.

413
00:23:43,040 --> 00:23:44,120
What?

414
00:23:44,200 --> 00:23:45,440
You can do that?

415
00:23:46,160 --> 00:23:47,840
A special service just for you.

416
00:23:49,200 --> 00:23:51,040
I want to know, fortune teller.

417
00:23:52,480 --> 00:23:54,080
When the time comes,
the universe will tell you.

418
00:23:56,120 --> 00:23:57,560
You don't say.

419
00:23:58,200 --> 00:23:59,840
Let's go somewhere to unwind.

420
00:23:59,920 --> 00:24:02,240
I know a place.
I'll send you the location.

421
00:24:07,080 --> 00:24:09,200
Fine. Don't tell me, then.

422
00:24:10,680 --> 00:24:11,920
I'll just go check it out myself.

423
00:24:33,160 --> 00:24:34,720
Morning.

424
00:24:34,800 --> 00:24:36,040
Min, Yihwa.

425
00:24:36,120 --> 00:24:37,800
Morning, Lee.

426
00:24:42,840 --> 00:24:44,400
What's going on with those two?

427
00:25:04,000 --> 00:25:06,440
Why is the vibe so tense today?

428
00:25:08,000 --> 00:25:10,320
Min and Yihwa are on their period.

429
00:25:11,560 --> 00:25:12,400
At the same time?

430
00:25:12,480 --> 00:25:13,920
Yeah.

431
00:25:27,600 --> 00:25:28,600
Are you on your period too?

432
00:25:29,640 --> 00:25:30,640
You seem pretty tense.

433
00:25:34,280 --> 00:25:35,760
Me? Tense?

434
00:25:37,160 --> 00:25:38,680
I wasn't that tense at first.

435
00:25:39,600 --> 00:25:40,880
But now I definitely am.

436
00:25:43,640 --> 00:25:45,440
If something's bothering you, just say it.

437
00:25:48,440 --> 00:25:50,800
Is there anything you're not telling me?

438
00:25:54,720 --> 00:25:55,720
Well…

439
00:25:58,600 --> 00:25:59,440
No.

440
00:26:03,160 --> 00:26:04,960
Then let me ask you this.

441
00:26:05,840 --> 00:26:08,800
You and Putter…
You're really not together, right?

442
00:26:18,080 --> 00:26:19,440
Are you suspicious of me?

443
00:26:20,360 --> 00:26:22,240
It's just that you seem…

444
00:26:22,320 --> 00:26:23,880
to care about him a lot.

445
00:26:27,200 --> 00:26:28,560
Of course I'm close to him.

446
00:26:28,640 --> 00:26:31,600
He's the one who reports
everything to my mom.

447
00:26:32,160 --> 00:26:34,080
So I have to stay on his good side.

448
00:26:35,680 --> 00:26:36,680
I get it.

449
00:26:38,200 --> 00:26:40,920
You think I'm closer to him
than I am to you, don't you?

450
00:26:45,560 --> 00:26:47,800
Hey, don't! Fuck, don't!

451
00:26:47,880 --> 00:26:48,760
Stop it!

452
00:26:48,840 --> 00:26:50,200
Ugh!

453
00:26:50,280 --> 00:26:52,120
I seriously can't take

454
00:26:52,200 --> 00:26:53,720
your straight-guy horseplay anymore.

455
00:26:53,800 --> 00:26:55,280
I take it back.

456
00:26:56,280 --> 00:26:57,280
I'm sorry.

457
00:26:59,120 --> 00:27:00,560
That's so gross.

458
00:27:03,400 --> 00:27:05,480
<i>What time today?</i>

459
00:27:09,880 --> 00:27:12,560
<i>3:40 pm. Meet me at the school gate.</i>

460
00:27:20,400 --> 00:27:21,800
Hey, Lee.

461
00:27:21,880 --> 00:27:23,920
You're walking like you're running
from the disciplinary office.

462
00:27:24,000 --> 00:27:26,520
I have to hurry. Someone might see us.

463
00:27:28,480 --> 00:27:29,800
And our date will be ruined.

464
00:27:30,400 --> 00:27:32,000
Oh, come on.

465
00:27:32,080 --> 00:27:33,840
There are plenty of other days.
We can go another time.

466
00:27:33,920 --> 00:27:35,360
But I promised.

467
00:27:50,440 --> 00:27:52,680
Hey, where are you two rushing off to?

468
00:27:52,760 --> 00:27:53,800
Where are you guys going?

469
00:27:54,520 --> 00:27:56,960
- We're going to study.
- You? Studying?

470
00:27:57,040 --> 00:27:58,200
LeeIth? Studying?

471
00:27:59,440 --> 00:28:00,960
You're actually getting serious.

472
00:28:01,040 --> 00:28:02,840
- I'm proud of you.
- Yeah, yeah.

473
00:28:02,920 --> 00:28:04,600
We're in a hurry.
We've gotta go or we'll be late.

474
00:28:04,680 --> 00:28:07,240
- Okay, see you on club day.
- See you on club day.

475
00:28:07,320 --> 00:28:08,320
Club day?

476
00:28:09,200 --> 00:28:11,040
Shit… Lee, Ter, wait!

477
00:28:11,920 --> 00:28:13,200
Shit, I just remembered something!

478
00:28:13,280 --> 00:28:15,520
Come back here, both of you!

479
00:28:15,600 --> 00:28:18,160
Mayday! Mayday!
Emergency meeting right now!

480
00:28:18,240 --> 00:28:20,600
Anyone who's already gone home,
get back to school now!

481
00:28:20,680 --> 00:28:21,800
I just remembered something!

482
00:28:21,880 --> 00:28:24,280
- Can it wait until another day?
- No, it has to be today!

483
00:28:25,000 --> 00:28:25,840
Shit…

484
00:28:25,920 --> 00:28:27,320
If we don't do it today,

485
00:28:27,400 --> 00:28:28,800
our club will be shut down!

486
00:28:28,880 --> 00:28:30,200
Move it!

487
00:28:30,880 --> 00:28:31,960
Hurry!

488
00:28:34,240 --> 00:28:36,200
- I'm hurrying already!
- Come on, hurry!

489
00:28:36,280 --> 00:28:37,680
Hey, careful! Don't spill it!

490
00:28:38,600 --> 00:28:40,960
We're supposed to submit the video today,

491
00:28:41,040 --> 00:28:42,240
or our club will lose points.

492
00:28:42,320 --> 00:28:43,200
- What?
- What?

493
00:28:43,280 --> 00:28:44,840
Why are you only telling us today?

494
00:28:44,920 --> 00:28:46,240
Actually…

495
00:28:46,320 --> 00:28:48,560
the teacher told us ages ago.
But I forgot.

496
00:28:48,640 --> 00:28:50,680
Didn't you write it down
or set a reminder?

497
00:28:50,760 --> 00:28:52,520
I stored it in my brain,
but then I forgot.

498
00:28:52,600 --> 00:28:53,720
Dumbass.

499
00:28:53,800 --> 00:28:55,120
Come on.

500
00:28:55,200 --> 00:28:56,120
Forget it for now.

501
00:28:56,200 --> 00:28:57,640
Let's figure it out first.

502
00:28:57,720 --> 00:28:58,640
No need.

503
00:28:58,720 --> 00:29:00,560
I've already thought of
my punishment for forgetting.

504
00:29:01,240 --> 00:29:03,280
Then why didn't you say so from the start?

505
00:29:03,360 --> 00:29:04,880
If I didn't hook you first,
would you listen?

506
00:29:04,960 --> 00:29:05,920
Stop dragging it out.

507
00:29:06,000 --> 00:29:07,600
- Let's go.
- Hey, wait!

508
00:29:09,360 --> 00:29:10,600
Hold on.

509
00:29:11,680 --> 00:29:12,680
Hello, where are you?

510
00:29:12,760 --> 00:29:14,480
<i>Hello, Bro. I'm here. Over this way!</i>

511
00:29:14,560 --> 00:29:17,840
- I'm here, Bro!
- Hurry up!

512
00:29:17,920 --> 00:29:19,000
What's up, Bro?

513
00:29:19,080 --> 00:29:21,920
Okay, we're filming a video exposing
the male students

514
00:29:22,000 --> 00:29:23,280
living at an all-girls school

515
00:29:23,360 --> 00:29:26,240
to promote our school
so more male students will apply.

516
00:29:26,320 --> 00:29:29,160
And then, the school can improve
the benefits for male students.

517
00:29:30,720 --> 00:29:32,360
I have to hand it to you
when it comes to content.

518
00:29:33,040 --> 00:29:34,200
Seriously, Bro. Seriously.

519
00:29:34,280 --> 00:29:35,960
That's awesome.

520
00:29:36,040 --> 00:29:37,320
So what's the plan?

521
00:29:37,400 --> 00:29:38,600
These days, it has to feel real.

522
00:29:38,680 --> 00:29:40,680
I want each of you to send me footage

523
00:29:40,760 --> 00:29:42,240
related to the school.

524
00:29:42,320 --> 00:29:44,520
I'll edit it, do the voice-over,
and that's it.

525
00:29:45,840 --> 00:29:46,760
Okay.

526
00:29:46,840 --> 00:29:48,880
- Go, go, go!
- Got it!

527
00:29:48,960 --> 00:29:51,080
Get in there! You too! Hurry up!

528
00:29:51,160 --> 00:29:52,000
Shoot plenty of it.

529
00:29:52,080 --> 00:29:53,720
Just in case we don't have enough content.

530
00:29:53,800 --> 00:29:55,160
Hurry up!

531
00:29:56,600 --> 00:29:58,280
Okay, everyone. I've turned on AirDrop.

532
00:29:58,360 --> 00:29:59,720
Send everything to my laptop.

533
00:30:04,840 --> 00:30:06,560
- I've already sent it.
- You already sent it?

534
00:30:08,160 --> 00:30:09,600
Yeah, I sent it.

535
00:30:15,200 --> 00:30:16,200
What?

536
00:30:17,800 --> 00:30:19,040
Whose footage is this?

537
00:30:23,040 --> 00:30:25,560
Judging by the order, isn't it LeeIth's?

538
00:30:28,760 --> 00:30:31,080
LeeIth has footage of Putter,

539
00:30:31,160 --> 00:30:33,760
and Putter has footage of LeeIth.

540
00:30:38,080 --> 00:30:39,360
What the hell are you guys staring at?

541
00:30:39,440 --> 00:30:43,000
Well, it's because we're roommates.

542
00:30:43,080 --> 00:30:44,360
Right? Aren't we?

543
00:30:44,960 --> 00:30:46,240
- Right? Yeah.
- Yeah, that's right.

544
00:30:47,120 --> 00:30:48,960
I think something's fishy.

545
00:30:50,760 --> 00:30:52,280
What the hell is so fishy about it?

546
00:30:52,360 --> 00:30:53,600
Prove it.

547
00:31:07,800 --> 00:31:08,760
Whoa!

548
00:31:14,040 --> 00:31:14,960
What?

549
00:31:15,040 --> 00:31:17,360
I kissed him to prove
we're strictly platonic.

550
00:31:21,080 --> 00:31:22,000
Don't!

551
00:31:23,440 --> 00:31:25,640
Hey, hey! That's enough!

552
00:31:26,560 --> 00:31:28,080
Get back to work, assholes.

553
00:31:29,240 --> 00:31:31,400
Come on, let's get this done.

554
00:31:33,160 --> 00:31:35,760
Hurry up, edit it, dub it,
so we can wrap it up.

555
00:31:55,560 --> 00:31:57,240
That's enough.

556
00:31:57,320 --> 00:32:01,560
I'm sorry for not keeping my promise.

557
00:32:01,640 --> 00:32:02,640
Mm.

558
00:32:03,160 --> 00:32:04,600
We can go another time.

559
00:32:04,680 --> 00:32:05,680
I'm not in a hurry.

560
00:32:08,280 --> 00:32:10,600
But I wanted to take you there today.

561
00:32:11,400 --> 00:32:12,600
I know.

562
00:32:12,680 --> 00:32:13,920
Let's save it for next time.

563
00:32:19,000 --> 00:32:20,960
If you could travel anywhere,
where would it be?

564
00:32:22,520 --> 00:32:23,600
Probably the beach.

565
00:32:24,760 --> 00:32:25,760
Oh,

566
00:32:26,320 --> 00:32:27,760
because Chiang Mai has no sea?

567
00:32:27,840 --> 00:32:28,880
Yeah.

568
00:32:28,960 --> 00:32:30,120
There are only mountains.

569
00:32:30,200 --> 00:32:31,200
I want to play in the water.

570
00:32:32,680 --> 00:32:35,080
Hey, I'll take you there.

571
00:32:35,160 --> 00:32:36,200
Come on.

572
00:32:38,640 --> 00:32:40,560
Hey, come on. Let's go.

573
00:32:41,160 --> 00:32:44,160
Ta-da! The Bangkok Sea. What do you think?

574
00:32:44,240 --> 00:32:45,360
Nice view, huh?

575
00:32:46,840 --> 00:32:48,640
A million-dollar view.

576
00:32:48,720 --> 00:32:50,600
For zero baht.

577
00:32:52,560 --> 00:32:53,800
Your mom paid for it, though.

578
00:32:57,280 --> 00:32:58,120
Way to kill the mood.

579
00:33:20,960 --> 00:33:22,200
Hey.

580
00:34:08,679 --> 00:34:09,840
Get in the water.

581
00:34:16,480 --> 00:34:19,000
Be careful. The waves are strong here.

582
00:34:44,320 --> 00:34:46,639
After you. This really feels like it.

583
00:34:52,360 --> 00:34:54,679
I'll let you pick the movie.
Today's Wednesday.

584
00:34:55,679 --> 00:34:57,120
Every movie is free.

585
00:34:59,840 --> 00:35:01,360
What a great deal.

586
00:35:02,720 --> 00:35:03,800
Then let's watch this one.

587
00:35:06,400 --> 00:35:09,560
It's a romance. Nice choice.

588
00:35:35,440 --> 00:35:36,800
If it were you,

589
00:35:38,480 --> 00:35:41,320
how would you confess to your friend?

590
00:35:43,680 --> 00:35:46,560
Well, I'd probably draw them a picture.

591
00:35:47,800 --> 00:35:50,240
So, you already confessed that day.

592
00:35:51,920 --> 00:35:53,080
You asked me to draw that day.

593
00:35:54,720 --> 00:35:56,240
But I wasn't drawing it for you.

594
00:35:57,400 --> 00:35:58,480
Way to kill the mood.

595
00:36:01,040 --> 00:36:02,120
You're getting cheesy again.

596
00:36:03,400 --> 00:36:05,200
You're really bad at playing it cool.

597
00:36:08,080 --> 00:36:11,000
All this time,
it's only worked because of me.

598
00:36:11,720 --> 00:36:12,800
No one suspected a thing.

599
00:36:15,120 --> 00:36:16,200
Nonsense.

600
00:36:30,440 --> 00:36:31,480
Let's watch this one.

601
00:39:17,840 --> 00:39:20,080
Talk about perfect timing.

602
00:39:21,200 --> 00:39:22,600
Hello, what's up?

603
00:39:22,680 --> 00:39:24,200
You're downstairs already?

604
00:39:24,800 --> 00:39:26,360
Shit, Indy's downstairs.

605
00:39:43,000 --> 00:39:45,720
MUSIC FESTIVAL

606
00:39:46,480 --> 00:39:47,800
Why didn't you answer my calls?

607
00:39:51,560 --> 00:39:52,520
I went…

608
00:39:55,040 --> 00:39:55,880
swimming.

609
00:39:56,800 --> 00:39:58,760
With Putter?

610
00:40:06,520 --> 00:40:07,600
It's okay.

611
00:40:08,200 --> 00:40:09,480
Can I apply?

612
00:40:09,560 --> 00:40:11,760
I secretly invited Proud too.
She's interested.

613
00:40:11,840 --> 00:40:12,880
Damn, Proud?

614
00:40:14,120 --> 00:40:16,080
Then sign up. What are you waiting for?

615
00:40:16,160 --> 00:40:18,160
So, should we discuss
which song to submit?

616
00:40:20,320 --> 00:40:21,400
Well…

617
00:40:23,960 --> 00:40:26,360
Or are you busy with something?

618
00:40:27,040 --> 00:40:28,720
Do you already have plans with Putter?

619
00:40:36,040 --> 00:40:37,640
No.

620
00:40:37,720 --> 00:40:39,200
You guys go ahead.

621
00:40:39,280 --> 00:40:40,640
I'm gonna play games.

622
00:40:40,720 --> 00:40:42,200
There are snacks in the fridge.

623
00:40:42,280 --> 00:40:43,520
Want some? I'll get them for you.

624
00:40:43,600 --> 00:40:44,640
Oh.

625
00:40:44,720 --> 00:40:45,720
It's okay.

626
00:40:46,440 --> 00:40:48,600
Oh, right. I was about to text you.

627
00:40:48,680 --> 00:40:50,680
You look cuter.

628
00:40:52,360 --> 00:40:54,480
You just look brighter.

629
00:40:55,360 --> 00:40:56,600
Are you in love or something?

630
00:40:59,640 --> 00:41:01,960
Thais really do talk nonsense. Go on.

631
00:41:02,040 --> 00:41:03,080
Come on, go sign up.

632
00:41:04,680 --> 00:41:07,200
Hurry up. Go to my room and practice.

633
00:41:08,720 --> 00:41:11,000
I'll make it up to you later.

634
00:41:21,560 --> 00:41:22,760
Hello.

635
00:41:25,240 --> 00:41:27,320
Don't hold your phone
so close to the speaker.

636
00:41:29,800 --> 00:41:31,000
My ears are killing me.

637
00:41:32,680 --> 00:41:34,880
Now then, a proper introduction.

638
00:41:34,960 --> 00:41:37,200
The newest member of Lazy Meow Meow.

639
00:41:37,280 --> 00:41:38,240
First up,

640
00:41:39,160 --> 00:41:41,200
our all-rounder drummer,

641
00:41:41,280 --> 00:41:43,720
a man of few words
but powerful beats, Leo!

642
00:41:47,240 --> 00:41:49,080
Next up,

643
00:41:49,800 --> 00:41:52,360
our bassist with slippery hands
and a slippery mind,

644
00:41:52,440 --> 00:41:53,920
Min.

645
00:41:54,000 --> 00:41:56,120
Give me a better nickname.

646
00:41:56,200 --> 00:41:57,320
Damn.

647
00:41:57,400 --> 00:42:00,160
That's so cool. That was insane, Min.

648
00:42:00,240 --> 00:42:02,240
The crazy part is we just found out
you can play, Min.

649
00:42:03,040 --> 00:42:04,040
Give us a song.

650
00:42:12,840 --> 00:42:15,680
Holy shit, that was incredible.

651
00:42:15,760 --> 00:42:18,280
Whoa, that's awesome! Come on.

652
00:42:18,360 --> 00:42:19,600
Let me join in.

653
00:42:23,040 --> 00:42:25,200
- Hey, everyone.
- Hey!

654
00:42:25,280 --> 00:42:26,680
Did Putter join the band too?

655
00:42:29,120 --> 00:42:30,360
No.

656
00:42:30,440 --> 00:42:32,880
Every band needs a manager, doesn't it?

657
00:42:32,960 --> 00:42:36,400
Taking photos and ordering food
for everyone. Isn't that good?

658
00:42:36,480 --> 00:42:39,520
It is. Then I can ship LeeIth and Putter.

659
00:42:40,760 --> 00:42:43,480
Stuff that overactive imagination back
into your head.

660
00:42:52,360 --> 00:42:53,840
Why didn't you tell me?

661
00:42:55,960 --> 00:42:58,720
It was supposed to be a surprise.
Wasn't it a good one?

662
00:43:00,320 --> 00:43:03,280
Come on, everyone. Let's play a song.

663
00:43:03,360 --> 00:43:04,800
Hey, film us for me.

664
00:43:04,880 --> 00:43:06,200
- Sure.
- Yeah, set up the camera too.

665
00:43:13,520 --> 00:43:15,880
<i>Wanna play with me?</i>

666
00:43:17,240 --> 00:43:19,520
<i>Been secretly watching you for so long</i>
<i>And you still don't know</i>

667
00:43:19,600 --> 00:43:22,240
<i>How many times</i>
<i>Have I seen you from right here?</i>

668
00:43:22,320 --> 00:43:24,880
<i>Every time you see a pup</i>
<i>You go play with it</i>

669
00:43:24,960 --> 00:43:26,840
<i>Yet with me, you act so indifferent</i>

670
00:43:26,920 --> 00:43:32,280
<i>How lucky to be born a dog</i>
<i>Getting all your love and care</i>

671
00:43:32,360 --> 00:43:35,000
<i>You only adore the pup</i>
<i>Nuzzling up for you to pet</i>

672
00:43:35,080 --> 00:43:37,360
<i>No need for approval</i>
<i>You love them right away</i>

673
00:43:37,440 --> 00:43:39,360
<i>I go to bed dreaming of being your pup</i>

674
00:43:39,440 --> 00:43:42,200
<i>So you can pet me before bed</i>
<i>Every single night</i>

675
00:43:42,280 --> 00:43:44,680
<i>Waiting at all hours</i>
<i>Keeping you from feeling sad</i>

676
00:43:44,760 --> 00:43:47,720
<i>Following you like a shadow</i>
<i>So you're never lonely</i>

677
00:44:12,560 --> 00:44:13,960
Putter.

678
00:44:16,000 --> 00:44:17,280
It's gorgeous.

679
00:44:23,680 --> 00:44:25,440
- You okay?
- I'm done.

680
00:44:25,520 --> 00:44:26,440
Look.

681
00:44:29,440 --> 00:44:31,600
Damn, you shoot so well.

682
00:44:32,560 --> 00:44:34,200
I've still got a lot to learn.

683
00:44:34,920 --> 00:44:36,120
<i>What are you doing today?</i>

684
00:44:36,200 --> 00:44:37,200
<i>Let's hang out.</i>

685
00:44:57,960 --> 00:44:59,400
<i>I'm busy today.</i>

686
00:44:59,480 --> 00:45:00,320
<i>Where are you going?</i>

687
00:45:06,520 --> 00:45:07,920
<i>What are you up to, my friend?</i>

688
00:45:10,440 --> 00:45:11,800
<i>I've got something to do.</i>

689
00:45:20,680 --> 00:45:23,600
Come on. Let's go for a walk. You in?

690
00:45:24,560 --> 00:45:25,560
- Let's go.
- Let's do it.

691
00:46:45,480 --> 00:46:47,680
So, does this make up for the beach?

692
00:46:49,280 --> 00:46:50,160
It does.

693
00:46:51,360 --> 00:46:53,960
<i>Oh, beautiful sea</i>

694
00:46:54,560 --> 00:46:56,720
<i>Beneath the bright blue sky</i>

695
00:46:58,080 --> 00:47:00,960
<i>I can see sailboats</i>

696
00:47:01,520 --> 00:47:03,240
And not just sailboats.

697
00:47:03,840 --> 00:47:07,520
There are speedboats,
banana boats, and soon, jet skis too.

698
00:47:07,600 --> 00:47:09,280
We'll work our way up,

699
00:47:09,360 --> 00:47:12,200
from a swimming pool, to the riverside,

700
00:47:12,280 --> 00:47:14,600
and next time, the sea for real.

701
00:47:16,120 --> 00:47:17,920
I hope you're not all talk.

702
00:47:39,600 --> 00:47:41,000
<i>Who's going to confess to Putter?</i>

703
00:47:41,760 --> 00:47:43,800
<i>When the time comes,</i>
<i>the universe will tell you.</i>

704
00:48:25,120 --> 00:48:28,200
<i>Since when did I start</i>
<i>feeling it this much?</i>

705
00:48:42,600 --> 00:48:43,960
DELETE POST

706
00:48:52,120 --> 00:48:55,280
SINCE WHEN DID I START
FEELING IT THIS MUCH?

707
00:49:37,040 --> 00:49:39,560
<i>The meaning of The Sun card.</i>

708
00:49:43,360 --> 00:49:44,800
<i>The truth will come to light.</i>

709
00:49:44,880 --> 00:49:47,160
<i>No secret in this world can stay hidden.</i>

710
00:50:14,440 --> 00:50:17,240
<i>Girl, I have some juicy gossip.</i>

711
00:50:37,480 --> 00:50:39,880
- Hi, LeeIth.
- You can pick the next song.

712
00:50:40,920 --> 00:50:43,840
- Hey, I want to pick the song.
- Deal.

713
00:50:44,680 --> 00:50:47,080
Next time, I'll choose my favorite song.

714
00:50:47,160 --> 00:50:48,000
Sure.

715
00:50:51,560 --> 00:50:52,520
Sure.

716
00:50:52,600 --> 00:50:53,920
Whatever Indy says, I'm in.

717
00:51:01,640 --> 00:51:02,880
What's wrong with you?

718
00:51:02,960 --> 00:51:04,280
Do you guys want anything
from the cafeteria?

719
00:51:04,920 --> 00:51:07,680
- Min, Yihwa, do you want anything?
- No.

720
00:51:13,640 --> 00:51:15,320
Are you mad at me?

721
00:51:15,400 --> 00:51:17,040
If you've got something to say,
just say it.

722
00:51:18,440 --> 00:51:20,200
I always say things straight.

723
00:51:20,280 --> 00:51:22,360
And when have you
ever been straight with me?

724
00:51:23,120 --> 00:51:24,560
Then ask me.

725
00:51:24,640 --> 00:51:26,360
Then why did you lie to me

726
00:51:26,440 --> 00:51:27,800
about going sketching with Putter?

727
00:51:29,760 --> 00:51:31,040
Why did you say you were busy?

728
00:51:39,120 --> 00:51:41,120
Just calm down first.

729
00:51:41,920 --> 00:51:44,000
I don't have a problem
with your new friend.

730
00:51:44,080 --> 00:51:46,840
I just don't get what the hell
is wrong with you.

731
00:51:50,640 --> 00:51:51,800
It's not about a new friend.

732
00:51:51,880 --> 00:51:53,360
It's not about a new friend.

733
00:51:53,440 --> 00:51:55,120
It's about you.

734
00:51:55,200 --> 00:51:57,120
If you don't want to be
friends with me anymore,

735
00:51:57,200 --> 00:51:58,960
then just say it, damn it.

736
00:52:14,920 --> 00:52:16,840
I'll go talk to Indy.

737
00:52:18,000 --> 00:52:20,040
I don't want you two
to end things like this.

738
00:52:25,000 --> 00:52:26,000
No.

739
00:52:26,720 --> 00:52:30,000
I think I need to handle this myself.

740
00:52:31,200 --> 00:52:32,560
Why?

741
00:52:34,200 --> 00:52:37,840
Because I'm the one who made that rule.

742
00:52:42,080 --> 00:52:46,480
And this evening,
I'll tell everyone in the club about us.

743
00:52:50,640 --> 00:52:52,000
Then we'll go together.

744
00:52:53,640 --> 00:52:55,240
It's not just your responsibility.

745
00:53:01,440 --> 00:53:02,560
Don't worry.

746
00:53:03,400 --> 00:53:04,840
I'll see you at the club this evening.

747
00:54:10,640 --> 00:54:12,200
- Tungtae! Tungtae!
- Tungtae! Tungtae!

748
00:54:12,280 --> 00:54:14,040
- LeeIth's over here, Bro!
- LeeIth's over here!

749
00:54:14,600 --> 00:54:15,760
Damn it, LeeIth!

750
00:54:17,920 --> 00:54:20,200
- Get up!
- What the hell are you sitting here for?

751
00:54:20,280 --> 00:54:21,280
Have you seen it?

752
00:54:21,360 --> 00:54:23,480
Those delusional idiots found
Putter's private account.

753
00:54:24,160 --> 00:54:26,360
And it looks like he has a thing for Indy.

754
00:54:28,040 --> 00:54:29,960
How do you know it's Putter's?

755
00:54:30,040 --> 00:54:33,280
Min told Summer that

756
00:54:33,360 --> 00:54:35,320
Putter typed a message,

757
00:54:35,400 --> 00:54:36,800
but accidentally posted it
to the wrong account.

758
00:54:36,880 --> 00:54:38,560
Then he deleted it and reposted it
on his private account.

759
00:54:38,640 --> 00:54:40,960
But someone was following
that private account.

760
00:54:41,480 --> 00:54:42,600
It was the exact same message,

761
00:54:42,680 --> 00:54:44,040
so they figured it out.

762
00:54:44,120 --> 00:54:45,880
Then they started screenshotting it
and shipping them.

763
00:54:45,960 --> 00:54:47,920
But it might not be him, LeeIth.

764
00:54:48,000 --> 00:54:49,160
What do you think?

765
00:54:52,440 --> 00:54:54,120
<i>You're not fast enough to avoid my eyes.</i>

766
00:54:54,200 --> 00:54:57,440
<i>#IndyPutterIsTheRealDeal</i>

767
00:54:57,520 --> 00:55:00,480
<i>It’d be nice if</i>
<i>you asked the right person.</i>

768
00:55:00,560 --> 00:55:01,720
<i>What is it?</i>

769
00:55:01,800 --> 00:55:03,480
<i>It's not this one.</i>

770
00:55:05,080 --> 00:55:06,200
Sorry, Putter.

771
00:55:06,280 --> 00:55:07,800
Yeah, it's okay.

772
00:55:07,880 --> 00:55:09,000
You're not gonna roast him?

773
00:55:09,080 --> 00:55:09,920
Indy.

774
00:55:10,000 --> 00:55:11,240
Three girls.

775
00:55:11,920 --> 00:55:12,960
Is that a new perfume?

776
00:55:14,040 --> 00:55:15,560
Indy wears the same scent.

777
00:55:19,320 --> 00:55:20,960
- Hey, Putter.
- Hey, Putter.

778
00:55:21,040 --> 00:55:23,440
- Putter!
- Putter!

779
00:55:26,120 --> 00:55:27,360
You're freaking awesome.

780
00:55:27,440 --> 00:55:29,320
- Yeah, seriously.
- Awesome!

781
00:55:29,400 --> 00:55:30,560
What are you talking about?

782
00:55:30,640 --> 00:55:32,080
You still don't get it?

783
00:55:33,680 --> 00:55:34,960
I know now.

784
00:55:36,000 --> 00:55:37,280
I know your secret.

785
00:55:38,240 --> 00:55:40,920
<i>‪All we can be is friends</i>

786
00:55:41,000 --> 00:55:44,680
<i>‪The one you love is definitely not me</i>

787
00:55:44,760 --> 00:55:51,400
<i>Time to stop dreaming</i>
<i>I never mattered to you</i>

788
00:55:51,480 --> 00:55:52,720
<i>So all this time</i>

789
00:55:53,600 --> 00:55:54,880
<i>you've liked Indy?</i>

790
00:56:17,880 --> 00:56:19,960
LeeIth, just hear me out.

791
00:56:20,040 --> 00:56:21,960
I can't date someone
who has a crush on my best friend.

792
00:56:26,480 --> 00:56:27,840
Indy!

793
00:56:29,000 --> 00:56:31,440
We know about you and LeeIth.

794
